              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "17993516"
            }
          ],
          "value": "The N-terminus has a gamma-class carbonic anhydrase-like domain (CA), while the C-terminus has 4 repeats that are similar to the small subunit of RuBisCO (rbcS), called SSUL. The SSUL are connected by flexible linkers. The N-terminal domain forms a scaffold on which CA and other carboxysomal proteins assemble, while the C-terminus binds RuBisCO"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DOMAIN"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "17993516"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Multiple forms of the protein of 73 (full length), 62, 52 (the most predominant form) and 36 kDa are seen even in the presence of protease inhibitors. CcmM52 interacts with CcaA"
        }
      ],
